-- Statements and bindings
--
-- A program is `name = expr;` bindings followed by the final expression.
-- Each value compiles once into the IR graph and every use of the name is
-- that node — no desugared lambda, so the root stays the final expression
-- and the program checks like a bare one.
-- output: 1

a = [1, 2]; 
b = 0; 
a[b]
